on on April 16, 1889. As a young boy, he played in music halls doing funny pantomimes. In 1910 he went to the U.S. to tour and decided to stay there. He acted in his first silent movie in 1914 as the world-famous character, \"the little tramp\". Chaplin consistently appeared as the little tramp in more than seventy movies."}, {"time": "41500", "image": "engenn6le06ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "His costume was a little hat, tight coat, baggy pants, big shoes, and a cane. His humor and sensitivity made audiences all over the world love him. His character became the symbol of the little man whose life was full of problems. Have you heard of \u201cthe little tramp\u201d?"}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "picture", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn6le06ob05re6img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn6le06ob05re6aud06", "images": []}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 3, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "picture", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn6le06ob05re5img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn6le06ob05re5aud01", "images": []}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 4, "_data": []}]}]}